Kinnerasani River:
{{Short description|River in India}}
{{redirect|Kinnerasani|wildlife sanctuary|Kinnerasani Wildlife Sanctuary}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=August 2019}}
{{Use Indian English|date=August 2019}}
The '''Kinnerasani''' is an important tributary of [[Godavari River]] flowing through the [[Warangal]] and [[Bhadradri Kothagudem district|Bhadradri]] districts of [[Telangana]] and [[Eluru district]] of [[Andhra Pradesh]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://www.telanganatourism.gov.in/nk-kinnerasani-dam.html |title=Kinnerasani Dam -- Telangana Tourism |access-date=16 October 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151023061524/http://www.telanganatourism.gov.in/nk-kinnerasani-dam.html |archive-date=23 October 2015 |url-status=dead }}</ref>
[[File:Kinnarsani Dam 08.JPG|thumb|300px|Kinnersani Dam built on the river near [[Paloncha]]]]
In the Khammam District, a dam known as the Kinnerasani Dam is built on this river. The backwaters of the dam are surrounded by verdant hills and come to be protected under the precincts of the [[Kinnerasani Wildlife Sanctuary]]. The gross storage capacity of the dam is 237.8 million cubic meters (Mcm) or 8.4 tmc ft <ref> National register of large Dams, Central Water Commission, Govt of India, 2019 Ed</ref>
The river drains on the right bank of [[Godavari]] in Telangana and forms common boundary between Andhra Pradesh and Telangana states before its confluence with main Godavari river.

