'''Himayat Sagar '''is an artificial lake about {{convert|20|km}} from [[Hyderabad]] in the [[Ranga Reddy district]] of [[Telangana]], India. It lies parallel to a larger artificial lake called [[Osman Sagar]]. The storage capacity of the reservoir is 84,016 [[cubic metre]]s.<ref>{{cite news|title=Hyderabadis can bid goodbye to water woes|url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Hyderabad/Hyderabadis-can-bid-goodbye-to-water-woes/article15478089.ece|newspaper=The Hindu|date=10 October 2016|access-date=11 October 2016}}</ref>

== History ==
The construction of reservoirs on the Esi, a tributary of the [[Musi River, India|Musi River]], was completed in 1927, with the intention of providing a drinking water source for [[Hyderabad, India|Hyderabad]] and protecting the city from floods, which Hyderabad suffered in 1908. It was built during the reign of the last Nizam of Hyderabad, [[Osman Ali Khan|Nizam VII]] and is named after his eldest son [[Azam Jah|Himayat Ali Khan]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.exploretelangana.com/history-of-osman-sagar-and-himayat-sagar-lakes-of-hyderabad-hyderabad-tourism/ | title=History of Osman Sagar and Himayat Sagar Lakes of Hyderabad – Hyderabad Tourism | date=14 September 2014 | access-date=9 December 2018 | archive-date=12 February 2019 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190212212945/http://www.exploretelangana.com/history-of-osman-sagar-and-himayat-sagar-lakes-of-hyderabad-hyderabad-tourism/ | url-status=dead }}</ref>

The Himayat Sagar dam and [[Osman Sagar]] [[reservoir]]s provided continuous water supply to the twin cities of Hyderabad and [[Secunderabad]] until recently. Due to population growth, they are not sufficient to meet the cities' water supply-demand.

The engineer at the time of construction was late Khaja Mohiuddin, son of Mohammed Hussein, Madri.{{citation needed|date=December 2018}}
[[File:Himayat Sagar Lake with Common Coots in Hyderabad W IMG 8638.jpg|thumb|210px|left|Himayat Sagar Lake]]
In 2022, the descendant of the royal family of the Nizam, Himayat Ali Mirza, joined the movement to save Osman Sagar and Himayat Sagar" as he believes that these reservoirs are iconic landmarks of Hyderabad and still act as a lifeline for lakhs of people of the old city. He also urged the then-CM of Telangana to withdraw the repeal of GO 111.<ref>{{Cite web |author=Syed Akbar|date=Mar 28, 2022 |title=nizam: Nizam's Kin Joinsfight To Save Lakes {{!}} Hyderabad News – Times of India |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/hyderabad/nizams-kin-joinsfight-to-save-lakes/articleshow/90482234.cms |access-date=2022-04-05 |website=The Times of India |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=March 28, 2022 |title=Nizam's Kin Joins fight To Save Lakes |work=[[The Times of truth]] |url=https://www.thetimesoftruth.com/nizam-nizams-kin-joinsfight-to-save-lakes-hyderabad-information/}}{{dead link|date=March 2025|bot=medic}}{{cbignore|bot=medic}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Nizam's relatives have joined the struggle to save Hyderabad's lakes. |url=https://thetimesbureau.com/nizams-relatives-have-joined-the-struggle-to-save-hyderabads-lakes-202203/ |access-date=2022-06-17 |website=thetimesbureau.com}}</ref>

If GO 111 is repealed, Himayat feared that many parts of the city might be affected by [[flood]]s even with small summer rains. Also, it would increase the illegal construction activities near the lake, ultimately increasing the threat of flooding.<ref>{{Cite web |date=May 9, 2022 |first=Akbar|last=Syed|title=Old city: 'repeal Of Go 111 To Spell Old City's Flood Threat' |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/hyderabad/repeal-of-go-111-to-spell-old-citys-flood-threat/articleshow/91425696.cms |access-date=2022-06-15 |website=The Times of India |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2022-04-23 |title=Explained: What is GO 111, the order to protect Hyderabad's Osman Sagar and Himayat Sagar, that has now been lifted |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/explained/go-111-order-to-protect-hyderabad-osman-sagar-himayat-sagar-lifted-7882177/ |access-date=2022-06-17 |website=The Indian Express |language=en}}</ref> In December 2023, the current Chief Minister [[A.Revanth Reddy]] decided to keep on hold the repeal of GO 111.<ref>{{Cite web |title=GO 111 Repeal Put on Hold by Revanth |url=https://www.deccanchronicle.com/nation/current-affairs/161223/go-111-repeal-put-on-hold-by-revanth.html}}</ref>

== Parks and conservation areas ==
The area surrounding the Himayat Sagar reservoir forms a critical [[Ecological restoration|ecological buffer zone]] for Hyderabad, featuring several protected green spaces, parks, and wildlife areas that mitigate the impacts of rapid [[Urban sprawl|urban expansion]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite journal |last=Das |first=Diganta |last2=Skelton |first2=Tracey |date=2019 |title=Hydrating Hyderabad: Rapid urbanisation, water scarcity and the difficulties and possibilities of human flourishing |journal=Urban Studies |volume=57 |issue=7 |pages=1553–1569 |doi=10.1177/0042098019838481}}</ref> These recreational and ecological sites serve both as public amenities and as urban biodiversity hotspots:<ref name=":1">{{Cite journal |last=Chan |first=Lena |date=2024 |title=Cities in nature |journal=Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society B: Biological Sciences |volume=379 |issue=1893 |doi=10.1098/rstb.2022.0322}}</ref>

* '''Kothwalguda Eco Park:''' Developed by the [[Hyderabad Metropolitan Development Authority]] (HMDA) adjacent to the reservoir, this 85-acre (34 ha) eco-tourism facility features a 1.5-kilometre (0.93 mi) elevated wooden boardwalk—the longest in India—that overlooks the landscape and provides panoramic views of Himayat Sagar. Its primary ecological attraction is the [[Kothwalguda Eco Park|Deccan Birds Aviary]]—a 6-acre dome-shaped, walk-through enclosure that houses over 6,500 exotic birds is the largest [[aviary]] in the world. The park also features a variety of themed botanical spaces, including a [[Japanese garden]], a [[rock garden]], and a butterfly zone.<ref name=":kothwalguda">{{Cite news |last=Singh |first=S. Bachan Jeet |date=2025-01-01 |title=Kothwalguda eco park to be inaugurated soon in Hyderabad |work=The New Indian Express |url=https://www.newindianexpress.com/cities/hyderabad/2025/Jan/01/kothwalguda-eco-park-to-be-inaugurated-soon-in-hyderabad}}</ref><ref name=":etv">{{Cite news |date=2026-03-11 |title=Hyderabad Gets a Massive Eco Park With 6,500 Birds, Boardwalk Trails And Recreational Zones |work=ETV Bharat |url=https://www.etvbharat.com/en/lifestyle/hyderabad-new-eco-park-kothwalguda-travel-enn26031104335}}</ref>
* '''Mrugavani National Park:''' Situated in close proximity to the Himayat Sagar reservoir near [[Chilkur, Ranga Reddy district|Chilkur]], this national park spans an area of approximately 1,211 acres (4.90 km²). It serves as a prominent wildlife refuge and conservation zone, and is home to a wide variety of native Deccan flora and fauna, including [[chital]] (spotted deer), [[sambar deer]], and numerous species of resident and [[Bird migration|migratory birds]].<ref name=":2">{{Cite web |title=Central Zoo Authority -- list of rec zoos |url=https://zoosprint.org/index.php/zp/article/view/3119/2893 |last=Walker |first=S. |journal=Zoos' Print |volume=XIX |issue=8 |pages=2}}</ref>
* '''Himayat Sagar Mini Zoo / Deer Park:''' Located along the peripheral boundary of the lake, this mini-zoo and deer park functions as a specialized conservation enclosure aimed at maintaining native [[deer]] populations and raising environmental awareness among visitors.<ref name=":2" />
* '''Ecotourism and Local Reserves:''' The peripheral wetland habitats and small streams feeding into Himayat Sagar support native fish populations like ''[[Channa harcourtbutleri]]'' and various [[aquatic insect]] groups.<ref name=":3">{{Cite journal |last=Laskar |first=Boni Amin |last2=Adimalla |first2=Harikumar |last3=Kundu |first3=Shantanu |last4=Jaiswal |first4=Deepa |last5=Chandra |first5=Kailash |date=2023 |title=Genetic evidence on the occurrence of Channa harcourtbutleri (Annandale, 1918) in Eastern Ghats, India: first report from mainland India |journal=Journal of Threatened Taxa |volume=15 |issue=3 |pages=22834–22840 |doi=10.11609/jott.6894.15.3.22834-22840|doi-access=free }}</ref><ref name=":4">{{Cite journal |title=A Field survey conducted at Himayat Sagar and Miralam Tank |journal=ZSI e-News |volume=1 |issue=2 |pages=4 |date=2009 |url=https://zsi.gov.in/uploads/documents/importantLinks/english/2009_2.pdf}}</ref> The surrounding green cover acts as a necessary eco-barrier to control pollution run-offs into the city's drinking water source.<ref name=":0" /><br />
